{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> be a segment of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be located on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfeda3a25ef23d83703782a1e18d33cec1d52540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969206ed7f062e51b8d559a0d5a86c30a5f7ecbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points on one of the semicircles with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8b5db9ff00c554cedc81b37d6c23b268ce29f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf82a8315ad5262334901309a69398bac2303611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edaede21a615fa385f9f1dab8fbcb59e24ed721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }5 \\qquad \\text{(B) }5 \\sqrt{2}  \\qquad \\text{(C) }7 \\qquad \\text{(D) }7 \\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\text{(E) }12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"390\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can solve this with some simple coordinate geometry. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> be located on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31572a833f4041c91695248e85c6f3a17ed948fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />axis. The equation of semi-circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/8091cad109ac8fc15533dd4e247d2b0444a7dcb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-13)^2+y^2=13^2, y \\geq 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"21\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are both perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, they must have the same <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562c10f8b24113ca3cc4bb4cbe019562fe4a48ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x -$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> coordinate. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> into our semi-circle equation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd049e624a41c0df950b22dadf2257ee2ad9410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52f2821f1a68dc474c90d7acb0e279c7fca51c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. The distance formula on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99b68c5c52d8275e4e79ba34fe318a22f84af4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8, 12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> gives us our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034ef04cb754e60be239312850381fbb98195305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(1-8)^2 + (5-12)^2}=\\sqrt{2(7^2)}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 7\\sqrt{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"366\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P\">2002 AMC 12P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042808\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 254/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5721/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.554      1 -total\n 63.65%    9.263      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 34.84%    5.070      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26586:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042808 and revision id 270578. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}